DT methodology-validation pass verdict: FIX-FIRST — do NOT run the scissor sweep as specified.
Four structural flaws + fixes: (Q1) step-catch-rate on residual is an invalid proxy — lock FRR
on CORRECT answers, measure FPR on residual; (Q2) abstention vs forced baselines needs coverage-
matched/AURC, not a point metric; (Q3) single 0.5B Stage-0 cut is a guaranteed false-negative —
need a 0.5B+8B two-point derivative; (Q4) residual x-axis confounded — Intersection-Residual +
parse-conditioned + probe-disabled ablation. Four cheap falsification probes capture whether the
confounds are real before any GPU. This re-qualifies our earlier cheap "scissor closed" call:
the close used a protocol DT flags as false-negative-prone (the normalization-artifact finding
still stands). Bears on the TRM Phase-3 thesis (verifier-as-Q-head assumes the moat is real).

